diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 783e37c..c082fb6 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 
 | Area | Change |
 |---|---|
+| Plugin cleanup | **Removed two switched-off, slower experiments: the lookahead prefetch (`MOE_CACHE_LOOKAHEAD*`: -25 %, -12 %, -74 % decode on three models) and the AVX-512 IQ kernels (`MOE_CACHE_AVX512`: 0.60-0.77x of llama.cpp's on a Zen 4)**. Both were off by default, so no default changes; the plugin no longer reads those variables, and the stats snapshot has no `pf_*` fields. A patch copy is in `archive/plugin/`. |
 | Bundled llama.cpp | **Pin moved from b12207 to llama.cpp b12651** (commit f5e6915c2, released 2026-11-23; contains #32807 `copy all experts of a host weight shared by several nodes`; ggml 1.0.0, backend API 4; a first draft used the untagged commit 5bacb7c, b12651 is 9 commits newer). Needed for Inkling 2 Mini. The kits bundle OUR build of that commit (every patch built in and off); the temperature-0 identity check now compares it with an unpatched build of the same commit that CI builds itself. The Windows kit ships `ggml-moe-cache-api4.dll` next to the api2 and api3 ones. On our test PC (27B, 128k, one run per arm, forecast) decode speed of this kit stayed within 5 % of the previous kit in every band; no prompt-speed claim is made for the new build; the older b12207 official build stays available with `LLAMA_SERVER`; the manual `official` release fallback now downloads the official b12651 assets. |
 | Browser apps on another local port | With llama.cpp b12651, `--cors-origins localhost` (what the launcher sets for a plain server) means the same origin only: a browser chat app on another local port (e.g. `http://localhost:3000`) is answered 403 until you pass `--cors-origins http://localhost:3000` after `--`. The control page, agents (Hermes, OpenCode, Claude) and `curl` send no Origin and are unaffected. Found by the key check on the pin branch (CI identity run 45082151697); checked in CI, not by a real browser app. |
 | Models | **Inkling 2 Mini / Small (looped architecture) can be launched**: the plugin builds against the ggml 1.0 headers, the launcher recognises ggml 1.0 and the `inkling2_loop` architecture, and for such a model it places experts by how often they are read (the layers that run once go to the CPU first; a loop layer is read several times per token), uses a small `-ub 128` micro-batch (the position bias grows with context) and says each choice and its source. Your own `--n-cpu-moe`, `-ot`, `-ub` and `--exact` win. b12651 is the build the launcher's Inkling note names as carrying the support (an older llama-server answers '!!!!' and the launcher says so). For such a model the launcher also adds `--no-op-offload` (the staging copy of the shared loop-layer experts does not fit a small card); `MOE_CACHE_INKLING_OP_OFFLOAD=1` or your own `--no-op-offload` setting keeps your choice. The correct answer was checked on one 8 GB laptop (CUDA, one short prompt) with an earlier llama.cpp build that carries the support; it has not been checked on the bundled b12651 kit as a release result, and no speed figure is claimed for this model in this release. |
